#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Generate research/byd/batch10/REPORT_batch10.md and unresolved_questions.md (numbers computed from the Batch 10 outputs)."""
import csv, os, json, collections
HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)); B10 = f"{HERE}/batch10"
rd = lambda p: list(csv.DictReader(open(p, encoding="utf-8", newline="")))
st = json.load(open(f"{B10}/stats_batch10.json", encoding="utf-8"))
SA = rd(f"{B10}/source_audit.csv"); LG = rd(f"{B10}/source_lineage_graph.csv"); CA = rd(f"{B10}/colour_conflict_audit.csv"); MY = rd(f"{B10}/model_year_consistency.csv"); RQ = rd(f"{B10}/evidence_requirements.csv")
sc = st["status"]; tot = st["colour_records"]
flag = [r for r in MY if r["unresolved_year_difference"] == "YES"]
flag_groups = {(r["model_id"], r["colour_name_zh"]) for r in flag}
reasons = st["year_flag_reasons"]
b8d = rd(f"{HERE}/batch8/discovered_codes.csv")
scopes = st["code_support_scope"]; prop_share = 100 * scopes["NAME_PROPAGATED"] / (scopes["NAME_PROPAGATED"] + scopes["MODEL_LISTED_APPROX"])
top = [r for r in RQ if r["row_type"] == "COLOUR_REQUIREMENT"]
cls = st["source_classes"]
L = []; a = L.append
a("# Batch 10 - real-world evidence & source quality audit (BYD Group)")
a("")
a("## **No genuine OEM evidence was obtained in Batch 10.** VERIFIED_OEM = 0, VERIFIED_LABEL = 0, CORROBORATED = 0.")
a("")
a("No label photograph, dealer record, official paint-code statement or owner contribution exists in this project. This batch audits what we have, shows which apparent conflicts have visible explanations in the supplier text, and prepares the evidence kit. **Nothing was promoted, no conflict was closed, no earlier record was deleted.**")
a("")
a("## Required figures")
a("")
a("| # | Measure | Value |")
a("|---|---|---|")
a(f"| 1 | Colour records audited (all brands, all batches) | **{tot}** (`model_year_consistency.csv`) |")
a(f"| 2 | Source lineages | **{st['lineages_all']}** lineages across **{st['sources_audited']}** audited sources; **{st['paint_code_lineages']}** lineages carry vehicle paint codes (OEMatch+DipYourCar; Touch Up Paint Factory+Cartouch; Carross; Colour Tubes; CROP). None is OEM-grade; mutual independence of the five is **unproven** (they may share an unknown paint-database upstream) |")
a("| 3 | VERIFIED_OEM | **0** |")
a("| 4 | VERIFIED_LABEL | **0** |")
a("| 5 | CORROBORATED | **0** |")
a(f"| 6 | POSSIBLE / CONFLICTED colour records | **{sc.get('POSSIBLE', 0)} / {sc.get('CONFLICTED', 0)}** (plus UNVERIFIED {sc.get('UNVERIFIED', 0)}; PAINT_SYSTEM_REFERENCE: {len(b8d)} identifier rows, 0 colour records whose only candidates are references) |")
a(f"| 7 | Unresolved model-year differences | **{len(flag)} colour records** in **{len(flag_groups)} model x colour groups** ({reasons.get('supplier year range excludes this model year', 0)} where a supplier's year range excludes the record's model year; {reasons.get('matte/gloss codes present but record finish unknown', 0)} with gloss/matte codes but unknown finish; {reasons.get('no model year assigned to this colour record', 0)} with no model year assigned) plus era differences in 苍穹蓝 (BYL/F2/L32C 2015-2019 vs LAN) |")
a("")
a("## What the audit found (and corrects)")
a("")
a(f"1. **Source quality.** {cls.get('MANUFACTURER_CONTROLLED', 0)} sources are manufacturer-controlled (BYD, Fangchengbao, Denza, Yangwang sites, manuals, importer brochures) - **none contains a paint code**. {cls.get('RETAILER_TOUCHUP_PAINT', 0)} are retailer/touch-up sources (the only places codes appear), {cls.get('LICENSED_PAINT_SYSTEM', 0)} are licensed-paint-system or vendor pages (behaviour only), {cls.get('MEDIA_PORTAL_CATALOG', 0)} are Autohome-type catalogue pages and {cls.get('ENCYCLOPEDIA', 0)} encyclopedia pages (colour names/years only). **No independent professional paint database and no authorised-dealer source has been obtained.**")
a("2. **Lineage correction.** Batch 7 counted Touch Up Paint Factory and Cartouch separately. They share 12 codes and carry identical normalised colour names on all 12 (100%); Cartouch states Axalta sourcing. They are now merged as a *likely shared upstream* (heuristic: >=10 shared codes and >=90% identical names). OEMatch and DipYourCar remain merged (95% over 60 codes). Paint-code lineages therefore fall from six to five. No status changed because nothing was above POSSIBLE.")
a("3. **HB5 vs HB6 (亚特兰蒂斯灰) is probably a finish difference, not a disagreement.** Every supplier text with a finish tag labels HB6 *matte* (Carross '¤MAT', Touch Up Paint Factory 'MATT', OEMatch/DipYourCar 'Matt Metallic') and HB5 plain metallic. Batch 7 had framed the matte hypothesis as coming from one lineage; Batch 10 finds the HB6-matte label in three lineages. It is still **not evidence**: the catalogue's Chinese 亚特兰蒂斯灰 records carry no finish information, BYD's importer brochures give none, and Carross supports HB6 only for Seal **2022**.")
a("4. **HA4 vs HAN (攀岩灰) looks like name-lumping.** HA4 is tied to 时光灰 ('TIME GREY', pinyin 'Shi Guang Hui') by two lineages; Cartouch's rows list 'HAN, HA4' together under Harbour/Boulder/Time Grey. HAN is tied to both 贝贝灰 (Dolphin) and 'Boulder/Climbing Grey'. The conflict may be an artefact of multi-name rows - unresolved.")
a("5. **雪域白 codes come partly from a seven-name group.** Touch Up Paint Factory lists W36C/WA2/WA8/BYHB-00001 for a group named Bright/Great/Polar/Snow/Snowfield/Summit/White Pearl, so it does not isolate 雪域白. Carross lists W36C *and* WA2 together for 'SNOW WHITE-MET.' (Qin/Tang 2017-2024); CROP says W36C 'Xue Yu Bai Pearl'; OEMatch/DipYourCar say WA2 'Xue Yu Bai Pearl'. Equating Carross's English 'Snow White' with 雪域白 is an assumption (a search snippet suggests BYD's export material uses 'Aurora White' for 雪域白; I could not verify it - the brochure URL returned 404).")
a(f"6. **Name propagation.** {scopes['NAME_PROPAGATED']} of {scopes['NAME_PROPAGATED'] + scopes['MODEL_LISTED_APPROX']} colour-record/code links ({prop_share:.0f}%) have **no supplier listing for that model**; the code was attached by colour name alone. Supplier model matching used here is approximate (name prefix).")
a("7. **Denza hotline.** 950856 now appears on two separate Denza page elements (footer customer-service line and a 24-hour rescue line on the service-support page), which strengthens - but does not prove - that it is Denza's official number. This is contact information only.")
a("8. **Linghui (领汇).** Media/portal pages describe it as a BYD sub-brand launched in 2026 with models (e5, e7, e9, M9) reported as derived from Dynasty/Ocean models; no official site, manual or service page was found. Parentage or similar names are **not** evidence of shared paint codes.")
a("")
a("## Priority conflict audit (`colour_conflict_audit.csv`)")
a("")
a("| Colour | Competing codes | Supporting lineages (per code) | What explains it? | Status |")
a("|---|---|---|---|---|")
for g in [r for r in CA if r["row_type"] == "GROUP"]:
    codes = [r for r in CA if r["row_type"] == "CODE" and r["colour_zh"] == g["colour_zh"]]
    a(f"| {g['colour_zh']} | {g['competing_codes'].replace(' | ', ', ')} | " + "; ".join(f"{r['code']}: {r['n_lineages']}" for r in codes) + " | see assessment in the CSV (finish / year / name-lumping candidates; none proven) | **OPEN** |")
a("")
for g in [r for r in CA if r["row_type"] == "GROUP"]: a(f"- **{g['colour_zh']}**: {g['assessment']}")
a("")
a("## Top 20 highest-priority unresolved colours")
a("")
a("| Rank | Colour | Competing / candidate codes | Current state |")
a("|---|---|---|---|")
for r in top: a(f"| {r['rank']} | {r['colour_zh']} | {r['target'].replace('resolve ', '').replace('confirm ', '')} | {r['current_state']} |")
a("")
a("Ranking: the four colours you named first, then Batch 9 conflict score, number of conflicted records and core-model coverage. Popularity is a proxy (your priority series); no sales data exists in the repository.")
a("")
a("## Exact evidence needed to resolve each major conflict")
a("")
a("| Colour | Needed |")
a("|---|---|")
for r in top[:4]: a(f"| {r['colour_zh']} | {r['minimum_evidence']} |")
a("")
a("Rows 5-20 and the rules for every status are in `evidence_requirements.csv`. In every case a single vehicle resolves only its own model-year; a split by year, model, finish or market needs at least one vehicle per band. A dealer record or label photo may support VERIFIED_OEM/VERIFIED_LABEL for that vehicle only, and the conflict is then *reviewed*, not auto-closed.")
a("")
a("## Evidence kit (real-world workflow)")
a("")
a("`owner_request_zh/en.md` (label photograph request - no VIN, no assumed location, voluntary identity link: first 9 characters or the owner's own hash); `dealer_request_zh/en.md` (written VIN-based confirmation - VIN supplied only by the owner, in person, never collected by the researchers); `evidence_photo_checklist.md` (shots, redaction, GPS stripping, what makes a photo VERIFIED_LABEL-grade, and a guide to tell an OEM paint code from a VIN, date, part number or formula/system identifier). **No label location is claimed for any model.**")
a("")
a("## Other brands")
a("")
a("Official sources re-checked: Denza service-support page now readable (rescue hotline 950856; no paint information); Yangwang and Fangchengbao manual pages remain JavaScript apps with no static PDF list (their undocumented APIs were not called); no owner-manual PDF, authorised documentation or genuine label found for Denza, Yangwang, Fangchengbao or Linghui. Nothing inaccessible is claimed as inspected.")
a("")
a("## Next batch")
a("")
a("1. **Field evidence is the only way forward** - Batch 11 should ingest whatever the user or owners provide: call answers (Batch 9 script), label photographs and dealer records (this kit), the Baslac factual answers. Without them, further desk research will only add retailer copies.")
a("2. If a Seal or Han EV owner can take part, start with 亚特兰蒂斯灰 (finish decides HB5 vs HB6) and 雪域白 (W36C vs WA2).")
a("3. Desk work worth doing meanwhile: obtain BYD's official colour-name tables per model-year (Chinese configurators/brochures) to fix finish and year availability; this would shrink the model-year question without any paint code.")
a("")
a("## Limitations")
a("")
a("- Lineage merging is heuristic and deliberately conservative (it can only reduce the independent count).")
a("- Supplier model matching is approximate; supplier year ranges are the suppliers' own and unverified.")
a("- No photograph, dealer record or official paint statement was obtained; the label search (B10S03) found none.")
open(f"{B10}/REPORT_batch10.md", "w", encoding="utf-8").write("\n".join(L) + "\n")

U = []; u = U.append
u("# Unresolved questions (Batch 10)")
u("")
u("Every item is **unanswered by evidence** unless stated. Nothing here is a finding.")
u("")
u("## A. Priority colours")
u("")
for g in [r for r in CA if r["row_type"] == "GROUP"]:
    u(f"### {g['colour_zh']} ({g['competing_codes']})")
    u(f"- Which code is on a real vehicle of each catalogue model-year ({g['catalog_model_years'] or 'years unknown'})? **UNANSWERED**")
    if g["colour_zh"] == "雪域白": u("- Do W36C and WA2 describe two colours, two years/models, or two systems for one colour? Is WA8 real? What is `BYHB-00001`? Is Carross's 'Snow White' the same colour as 雪域白? **UNANSWERED**")
    if g["colour_zh"] == "攀岩灰": u("- Is HA4 a 时光灰 code that Cartouch lumped into Boulder-Grey rows? Do 贝贝灰 (Dolphin) and 攀岩灰 (Atto 3) share HAN? **UNANSWERED**")
    if g["colour_zh"] == "亚特兰蒂斯灰": u("- Does a matte Atlantis Grey exist in the Chinese market? Is every Chinese-market Seal HB5, HB6, or both by finish/year? **UNANSWERED**")
    if g["colour_zh"] == "苍穹蓝": u("- Do BYL/F2/L32C belong to 2015-2019 and LAN/L-27 to later years? Are the LAN listings 苍穹蓝 or 穹顶蓝 ('Dome Blue')? **UNANSWERED**")
    u("")
u("## B. Lineages")
u("")
u("- Are Touch Up Paint Factory and Cartouch really one upstream (12/12 identical names), and is that upstream Axalta? **UNANSWERED** (merged conservatively)")
u("- Are Carross, Colour Tubes and CROP independent of each other and of the others? Name overlap is partial (CROP-Carross 3/4, Colour Tubes-TUPF 4/7) - **UNPROVEN**")
u("- Does any retailer cite an OEM source? **No retailer does.**")
u("")
u("## C. Model-year")
u("")
u(f"- {len(flag)} colour records in {len(flag_groups)} model x colour groups carry a year question (see `model_year_consistency.csv`, column `unresolved_year_reasons`).")
u(f"- Which catalogue colour records have no model year assigned and why? ({reasons.get('no model year assigned to this colour record', 0)} records with candidate codes)")
u("- Supplier year ranges (e.g. Carross 2017-2024) are the suppliers' own; are they BYD production years? **UNKNOWN**")
u("")
u("## D. Real-world evidence")
u("")
u("- Does a factory colour label exist on any BYD model, and where? **UNANSWERED** (no official confirmation for any model)")
u("- Can a BYD service centre read the factory colour/code from a VIN and give it in writing? **UNANSWERED** (no call made; scripts in Batch 9)")
u("- Does BASF Baslac Formula Finder list BYD? **UNTESTED** (terms acceptance is the user's decision; no formula may be stored)")
u("")
u("## E. Other brands")
u("")
u("- Owner-manual PDFs for Denza, Yangwang, Fangchengbao: **NOT FOUND** (Yangwang and Fangchengbao pages are JavaScript apps).")
u("- Linghui official site/manual/service pages: **NOT FOUND**.")
u("- Denza/Yangwang paint or label documentation: **NOT FOUND**.")
open(f"{B10}/unresolved_questions.md", "w", encoding="utf-8").write("\n".join(U) + "\n")
print("report", len(L), "lines; unresolved", len(U))
